#: ../../docstring log.debug:3 log.error:5 log.info:3 log.trace:3 log.warn:3 of
msgid ""
"The four coordinates are keyword-only and optional; report, page and "
"activity come from the engine's spans and must not be passed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring log.error:1 of
msgid ""
"Something the extraction got wrong and did not silently absorb — an "
"accounting equation that does not balance, a row that had to be dropped. "
"Reaches `.log.csv`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring log.error:3 of
msgid ""
"It does **not** fail the pipe: raising an exception is how a pipe fails, "
"and keeping the two apart is what lets an algorithm report a bad row "
"without losing the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring log.info:1 of
msgid ""
"The course of the extraction, for someone watching the run. Never reaches"
" `.log.csv`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring log.trace:1 of
msgid ""
"The finest detail, for a page that has stopped adding up. Visible only at"
" `-vvv`, where it also lands in `freeports.log.jsonl`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring log.warn:1 of
msgid ""
"Something a reader of the data must know: a value imposed rather than "
"read, an assignment deduced from an ambiguity, something seen on the page"
" and not modelled. Reaches `.log.csv`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring log.warn_imposed:3 of
msgid ""
"The free-text functions above are the point of this module, and this one "
"is the counterweight: a recurring warning written by hand each time "
"becomes ten phrasings of one fact, and then nobody can find it in the "
"`.log.csv`. This is the only such helper that exists, because it is the "
"only wording the rules have already settled. The next one is added when a"
" phrasing has actually repeated itself, not in anticipation of it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring log.warn_imposed:9 of
msgid ""
"`field` fills `Second coord ref`, the column that says which field a row "
"is about."
msgstr ""

